- BPW: Average bits per weight across tensors (not including input embeddings, encoders, or output head)
- Size on disk: Total aggregate size of tensors in checkpoint, in GiB
- VRAM (exllamav3): Total VRAM consumption as typically used in exllamav3, in GiB (minus embeddings)
- VRAM (vLLM): Total VRAM consumption as typically used in vLLM, in GiB (blockq embeddings, offloaded/omitted encoders)
{% if composite %}- Excess KLD: how far each quant's next-token distribution is from the unquantized model's, minus the unquantized model's own rounding noise, so 0 would be indistinguishable from the original (lower is better). Measured on the model's own answers to real use: {% for sl, (n, w) in eval_slices.items() %}{% if sl == 'wild' %}real users' first prompts from WildChat-1M ({{ n }} conversations, many languages, about half with pasted material){% elif sl == 'swe' %}real coding-agent sessions from Open-SWE-Traces ({{ n }} sessions, each cut at a turn the model writes itself){% else %}{{ sl }}{% endif %}, weight {{ '{0:0.2f}'.format(w) }}{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}. The answers were generated by the unquantized model.
{% if show_ppl %}- Δ perplexity: change in perplexity on the same text, same weights (lower is better)
{% endif %}- Raw-text excess KLD: the same measure on plain web text with no chat template. It matches no real use and is a sanity check, not a ranking: a calibration tuned to conversations can trade a little here.
{% else %}- Raw-text excess KLD: how far each quant's next-token distribution is from the unquantized model's on plain web text, minus the unquantized model's own rounding noise (lower is better). This model has no chat template, so raw text is the distribution it was trained on.
{% endif %}
{% if composite %}
These quantizations are calibrated on a conversational mix rather than the bundled raw-text corpus: documents pasted into user turns and returned as tool results, short tool-use loops, a little of the model's own voice, and the default corpus. Its answers come from an uncalibrated 8-bit quant of the same model. Against the default calibration at equal size, it cut excess KLD on real user prompts by 12-13% on Qwen3.8-27B and 8-11% on Ornith-1.5-9B (4 bpw), at no cost in bytes ([details](https://github.com/yeasah/vllm-exl3-plugin/blob/main/docs/calibration.md)).
{% endif %}
